title: 'statement-store: resend statements a slow or failing peer missed'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    A peer that stops reading or whose sends fail no longer loses statements. A full
    propagation outbox now refuses new hashes instead of dropping its oldest, and a failed
    propagation send gives up its chunk and the rest of the outbox. In both cases the peer
    records the lowest admission sequence it missed. Once its outbox drains, an initial sync
    walks the admission journal from that sequence to the current watermark, so the peer
    receives every missed statement once, in admission order. Before, the dropped hashes and
    the failed chunks were never resent, and the peer got those statements only from another
    peer or a later full resync.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
